  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY NIGHT THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 210 PM CDT Tue Jul 21 2026\n\nA stronger wave looks to move across the top of the ridge by \nThursday evening and bring us our next chance for meaningful precip. \nInstability will be quite limited so severe weather is unlikely, \nthough some thunder is possible Thursday night into Friday morning \nin southern Iowa. The nocturnal LLJ returns to our vicinity during \nthe Thursday overnight, with the nose centered over southwest Iowa. \nThis should erode the dry air and allow the quite saturated mid \nlevels to rain down to the surface. The main story will be QPF \namounts. WPC has southwest Iowa in a marginal ERO for Thursday and \nFriday, and PWATs are well over 2 inches. There is a large QPF \nspread across the models, but a few give spots in southern Iowa 1-2 \ninches of rain. By the weekend, the ridge intensifies over the \nDakotas, bringing us another period of heat. We may breach the 90s \nagain on Saturday, and Sunday/Monday look to be the warmest as a \nmore substantial EML is advected in.",
